            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LDSGIRL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really great with a few minor tweaks. I looked over other greek salad recipes on this site and came up with the best dressing. Instead of 4 tsp. of lemon juice, add 3 and 1 tsp of red wine vinegar. For the salt and pepper, add 1/4 tsp of each. Also, add half a green pepper chopped, kalamata olives instead of black and it comes out amazing!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent salad! Stirred in just a couple heaping tbsp. of nonfat greek yogurt. I darn near ate the whole bowl. I might try it with the red wine vinegar in place of the lemon juice as other reviewers have suggested and see how that is. The longer it sits, the better it gets. NOTE: A trick Grandma taught me to help draw some of the liquid out of tomatoes is cut them the way you want them on the salad, then lay them on paper towels and sprinkle with salt. Let them sit for a bit and drain. Blot with paper towels. You do this, your salad will be less drippy.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-11T21:44:29.980Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MPEBLE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! Fresh, summery, and healthy. Next time I may try it with fresh herbs. All measurements are approximate in this recipe; suit to your taste. Tip: cut the cucumbers lengthwise, then scoop out the seeds with a spoon and discard. This keeps the salad from becoming to soupy and slimy, and gives it a crisper texture.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-16T21:17:50.247Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "passion8chef"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad turned out great. I halved everything using 2 roma tomatoes, 1/2 large cucumber, thinly sliced, 1/2 small purple onion, 1 1/2 T. olive oil, 2 tsp. lemon juice, 1/2 t. salt, 1/4 tsp black pepper, a pinch of organo, about 1/2 cup feta cheese and 6 olives, quartered. I whisked together the olive oil, lemon juice, salt &amp; pepper and tossed the cut up veggies to coat. I refrigerated the salad for about 30 minutes while I prepared the rest of dinner. Just before serving I added a couple of cups of chopped romain lettuce. It made 4 \"side dish\" servings. Definitely a recipe to use over and over again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-21T19:06:09.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Robbie Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My hubby was Greek, so I made a version of this salad often. His mom taught me to make it the Greeks do. This basic recipe will work. However, be sure to use kalamata olives (best in the world), and cut your feta into rectangular chunks instead of crumbles. Also, you can replace the lemon juice with a nice red wine vinegar. Some minced garlic added to the dressing is good, too.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-14T00:07:32.774Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nancy Linden"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this salad with apple cider vinegar instead of lemon juice. I whipped the oil, vinegar salt, pepper and oregano until creamy and poured it over the salad. Very good recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2022-02-27T19:07:51.499Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "veghead46"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I make it often. I have a Greek seasoning that I use for other recipes and this one too. That is one change I make. This basic recipe is versatile. I have added it to rotini noodles. In the summer I sometimes omit the tomatoes and core and open a large Jersey tomato and fill with the Greek salad !",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-13T17:45:40.049Z"
          },
          {
